title: AWS Lambda Function
agents: aws
catalog: cloud/aws
license: WTFPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors AWS Lambda function metrics via CloudWatch.
 It provides visibility into function performance and errors.

 Monitored metrics:

 - Duration (Average/Maximum): Execution time in milliseconds

 - Errors: Number of failed invocations

 - Throttles: Number of throttled invocations

 - Invocations: Total number of function invocations

 - Concurrent Executions: Maximum concurrent executions

 With the "Lambda Insights" service enabled in the agent rule (needs the
 Lambda Insights extension on the function), memory utilization, total and
 used memory, CPU time, network bytes, init duration and /tmp usage are shown
 in the service details as well.

 Shown in the service details only (no thresholds, graphed):
 Minimum duration, iterator age, dead letter errors,
 destination delivery failures, async events (received, age, dropped) and
 provisioned concurrency (executions, invocations, spillover, utilization).

 Thresholds can be configured for duration, errors, throttles,
 invocations, and concurrent executions.

discovery:
 One service is created for each active Lambda function discovered.
 Deleted functions stay until CloudWatch stops listing their metrics (up to
 2 weeks). They are hidden right away only with "Lambda: Hide deleted functions
 immediately" enabled in the agent rule (needs lambda:ListFunctions).
